Proposed fix (also from the AI): store the last processed offset per partition in the same transaction as the balance change, and skip any message whose offset is not greater.

BEGIN;
SELECT last_offset FROM consumer_offsets WHERE partition = 3;            -- 7709
UPDATE wallets SET balance = balance + 50 WHERE user_id = 'u-18';
UPDATE consumer_offsets SET last_offset = 7710 WHERE partition = 3;
COMMIT;

The outbox relay of the points service crashed between publish and mark, so event p-9001 was published twice: at offset 7702 and again at offset 7710.

Statement: "With this fix, the second copy of p-9001 at offset 7710 is skipped."
